<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  es-theme-xmb-psp - "Button Icons: Xbox".
  Selected via UI Settings > Theme Configuration > Button Icons > Xbox.

  For controllers in the Xbox / SDL layout: most USB and Bluetooth gamepads, and
  handhelds that follow the same ABXY ordering.

  Same four PNGs as the Nintendo set. The two layouts draw identical buttons
  and disagree only about where each letter goes, so this file is nothing but
  a different assignment of the same art:

      slot     position   Nintendo   Xbox
      iconA    EAST       A          B
      iconB    SOUTH      B          A
      iconX    NORTH      X          Y
      iconY    WEST       Y          X

  All four move. That is the point of shipping the set, and it is also why
  hardcoding one lettered set would have been wrong for half the theme's
  users rather than merely inauthentic.

  Slot -> physical position is fixed by ES; the derivation and the
  InvertButtons non-caveat are documented once in _inc/buttons-nintendo.xml.

  The glyphs are monochrome, not Xbox's colour-coded green/red/blue/yellow.
  ES tints every help icon through ImageComponent::setColorShift, which
  multiplies the texture by <iconColor> (${helpAccent} here), so four coloured
  sources would come out as four muddy shades of one hue rather than four
  colours. Monochrome line art is what section 5.1 of the style guide asks for
  anyway.

  CC-BY-NC-SA 2.0. See CREDITS.md.
-->
<theme>
  <formatVersion>7</formatVersion>
  <variables>
    <helpIconA>./art/help/btn-b.png</helpIconA>
    <helpIconB>./art/help/btn-a.png</helpIconB>
    <helpIconX>./art/help/btn-y.png</helpIconX>
    <helpIconY>./art/help/btn-x.png</helpIconY>
  </variables>
</theme>
